{
  "_readme": [
    "Human labels for the narrative judge. Each entry scores ONE narrative on the",
    "same three axes and the same 0/1/2 scale the judge uses, so the two can be",
    "compared directly (evals/judge.py::calibration).",
    "",
    "This file is hand-written and stays hand-written. It is the one artefact in",
    "the measurement layer that a model must never produce: its entire purpose is",
    "to be an independent check on a model's scoring, and a generated label set",
    "would be the judge marking its own homework one level up.",
    "",
    "Until it has entries, `sqe judge` reports its scores as UNCALIBRATED and does",
    "not claim them as a measurement of narrative quality. The grounding rate is",
    "unaffected either way -- that half is arithmetic, not judgement.",
    "",
    "To label: run `sqe judge --label --sample 20`, which prints one narrative at a",
    "time with its question and rows and writes your scores here. Label the sample",
    "it gives you rather than cherry-picking cases; a set biased toward narratives",
    "that looked wrong measures the judge on hard cases only and overstates its",
    "disagreement.",
    "",
    "The number that matters most on the far side is judge_lenient: cases the judge",
    "passed and you failed. A judge that is generous where a human is not cannot",
    "support a claim about narrative quality, whatever its per-axis agreement says.",
    "",
    "Axes, scored 0 (fails) / 1 (partial) / 2 (passes):",
    "  relevance    -- does it answer the question that was asked",
    "  faithfulness -- do its qualitative claims follow from the rows",
    "  calibration  -- does it claim causes, forecasts or significance the rows",
    "                  cannot establish",
    "",
    "Do NOT score arithmetic. Whether a figure appears in the rows is checked",
    "deterministically by evals/grounding.py; judging it here would make the",
    "calibration set disagree with the judge for a reason neither is wrong about.",
    "",
    "Entry shape:",
    "  {\"case_id\": \"b_revenue_by_region\", \"relevance\": 2, \"faithfulness\": 1,",
    "   \"calibration\": 2, \"reason\": \"calls the gap 'significant' on three rows\"}"
  ],
